@prefix agp: <https://dagalog.no/ns/agentprov#> .
@prefix bl: <https://dagalog.no/ns/backlog#> .
@prefix ghissues: <https://github.com/daghovland/rdf-datalog/issues/> .
@prefix ghpull: <https://github.com/daghovland/rdf-datalog/pull/> .
@prefix prov: <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix session: <https://dagalog.no/ns/agentprov/session#> .

# Timestamps below are real (from `git log
# 536e76b0fdfd26e6fd8f8cae3fff1c59aca3fbcc..HEAD` on branch
# feat/565-wire-backlog-snapshot).

ghpull:685 a bl:PullRequest, bl:WorkItem ;
    rdfs:label "Wire backlog snapshot into the production dataset" ;
    bl:number 685 ;
    bl:state bl:Open ;
    bl:closesIssue ghissues:565 .

session:claudeSonnet5 a prov:SoftwareAgent ;
    rdfs:label "Claude Sonnet 5" .

session:pr685 a agp:AgentSession ;
    prov:wasAssociatedWith session:claudeSonnet5 ;
    prov:used ghissues:565 ;
    prov:startedAtTime "2026-09-29T18:31:42Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    prov:endedAtTime "2026-09-29T19:04:34Z"^^xsd:dateTime .

session:pr685Summary a agp:TranscriptSummary ;
    agp:summaryText "Issue #565 (follow-up from #493) asked for a way to wire bl:/agp: instance data into production dagalog's --data /data/dataset.ttl, which nothing in the repo currently populates. Before writing anything, read the actual data/dataset.ttl on this host (read-only): it already contained a one-off, hand-built concatenation of the backlog ontology + a backlog-regenerate snapshot + provenance/summaries/*.ttl -- confirmed by an exact bl:CurrentSnapshot bl:generatedAt match against snapshot.ttl's Aug 11 header, ~7 weeks stale. That finding reversed the initial plan (add several more --data flags to docker-compose.public.yml, resolved via a container entrypoint script): layering a second --data source on the existing stale merge would double up bl:CurrentSnapshot/bl:Issue with conflicting bl:generatedAt/bl:Open/bl:Closed, breaking #380's staleness query. Fix instead: reproduce the hand-merge as scripts/regenerate-production-dataset.sh, writing data/dataset.ttl via temp-file + atomic rename (a failed gh api call never corrupts a working dataset), with --skip-regenerate/--no-restart for testability and --print-sources asserted (by test) to match serve-backlog.sh --print-data-args, so the two hand-maintained file lists can't silently diverge. backlog-regenerate gained a small --out <PATH> flag (unit-tested arg-parsing in backlog::regenerate_cli) so production never dirties the tracked snapshot.ttl from a scheduled job. An advisor review flagged that the plan's 'concatenation is safe' claim was asserted, not checked; grepped all sources for labeled blank nodes and relative-IRI/@base markers -- every hit traced to prose inside an agp:summaryText string literal (e.g. pr-669's _:x example, pr-419's <#service> mention), never real Turtle syntax, so the concatenation is genuinely safe, not assumed. Verified live, not just 'looks right': ran the real backlog-regenerate against a scratch --out path, which hit a transient GitHub API 500 twice before succeeding -- concretely confirming the script leaves --out untouched on failure -- then queried the merged file, getting a live same-day bl:generatedAt and 371 real bl:Issue rows. A first draft of this summary/PR body claimed this live run had already happened before it actually had; caught by a further advisor pass and corrected here. This host turned out to already run the production deployment itself (deploy-dagalog-1 etc, confirmed via docker ps) -- not 'no access', but a deliberate choice not to touch the real data/dataset.ttl or restart the live container from inside this PR, since that's Dag's own rollout call. Filed #687 (sub-issue of dashboard epic #378, Status Todo) for that rollout. Tests were written alongside the implementation, not ignored-first -- a deploy/infra task without a natural red/green cycle, not a deliberate TDD skip." ;
    agp:reasoningFor ghpull:685 ;
    agp:decisionPoint session:pr685Decision ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy session:pr685 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo session:claudeSonnet5 .

session:pr685Decision a agp:Decision ;
    agp:summaryText "Chose a host-side script that rebuilds one merged data/dataset.ttl file (matching the shape already found hand-built on this host) over two other options considered: (1) adding a second, separate --data file to docker-compose.public.yml's dagalog service -- rejected once the existing dataset.ttl was found to already contain the same data, since a second source would duplicate/conflict with bl:CurrentSnapshot and per-issue bl:Open/bl:Closed state rather than replace it; (2) a GitHub Actions cron job that regenerates and commits the snapshot back to main -- rejected because a bot pushing directly to main bypasses this repo's own PR-only workflow, a bigger design decision than this issue's scope, left as a documented-and-rejected alternative rather than silently omitted." ;
    agp:alternative "Second --data file layered on top of the existing (stale) merged dataset.ttl; a GitHub Actions cron job committing the regenerated snapshot to main." .
